+# tasks-api
+
+A multi-tenant task-tracking API built with [Bun](https://bun.sh), [Elysia](https://elysiajs.com) and [Drizzle ORM](https://orm.drizzle.team) on SQLite (via libSQL).
+
+Organizations own projects, projects own tasks, and users belong to one organization. Every authenticated request is scoped to the caller's organization.
+
+## Running locally
+
+Prerequisites: Bun 1.4.3 (pinned in `package.json` as `packageManager`).
+
+```sh
+# 1. Install dependencies
+bun install
+
+# 2. Configure the environment (Bun loads .env automatically)
+cp .env.example .env
+
+# 3. Create the database directory. The default DATABASE_URL points at data/dev.db,
+#    and migrations fail if the directory does not exist.
+mkdir -p data
+
+# 4. Apply migrations
+bun run db:migrate
+
+# 5. Load development fixtures
+bun run db:seed
+
+# 6. Start the dev server (restarts on file changes)
+bun run dev
+```
+
+The API listens on `http://localhost:4000` by default. Check it with:
+
+```sh
+curl http://localhost:4000/api/health
+# {"status":"ok"}
+```
+
+Notes:
+
+- The server also applies pending migrations at startup, so step 4 is only strictly needed before seeding.
+- The seed inserts fixed IDs, so running `db:seed` a second time against the same database fails. To start over, delete the database file (`rm data/dev.db`) and run migrate and seed again.
+- `bun run start` runs the server without file watching.
+
+### Seed data
+
+`bun run db:seed` creates two organizations. Every seeded user has the password `password123`.
+
+| User         | Email              | Org                   | Role   | Pre-issued API token     |
+| ------------ | ------------------ | --------------------- | ------ | ------------------------ |
+| Ada Lovelace | `ada@acme.test`    | Acme (`org_acme`)     | admin  | `dev-acme-admin-token`   |
+| Bob Builder  | `bob@acme.test`    | Acme (`org_acme`)     | member | `dev-acme-member-token`  |
+| Gina Globex  | `gina@globex.test` | Globex (`org_globex`) | admin  | `dev-globex-admin-token` |
+
+The pre-issued tokens are valid for ten years and are for local development and tests only. Acme has three projects (`prj_web`, `prj_app`, `prj_billing`) and Globex has one (`prj_infra`). There are six tasks in total (`tsk_1` to `tsk_6`).
+
+## Environment variables
+
+| Variable          | Default            | Description                                                                                                    |
+| ----------------- | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `PORT`            | `4000`             | HTTP port the server listens on.                                                                               |
+| `DATABASE_URL`    | `file:data/dev.db` | libSQL connection URL. Used by the server, `db:migrate`, `db:seed` and `drizzle-kit`.                          |
+| `WEBHOOK_SECRET`  | none               | Shared secret expected in the `x-webhook-secret` header. If unset, every webhook request is rejected with 401. |
+| `TOKEN_TTL_HOURS` | `24`               | Lifetime of tokens issued by `POST /api/auth/token`.                                                           |
+| `LOG_LEVEL`       | `info`             | One of `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`, `silent`. Logs are JSON lines on stdout/stderr.                       |
+
+## Scripts
+
+| Script                 | Purpose                                                             |
+| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `bun run dev`          | Start the server with file watching.                                |
+| `bun run start`        | Start the server.                                                   |
+| `bun run build`        | Bundle the server to `dist/`.                                       |
+| `bun run db:migrate`   | Apply migrations from `drizzle/`.                                   |
+| `bun run db:seed`      | Insert development fixtures.                                        |
+| `bun run db:generate`  | Generate a new migration from `src/db/schema.ts`.                   |
+| `bun run test`         | Run the Vitest suite. Each test uses a fresh, seeded temp database. |
+| `bun run typecheck`    | Type-check with `tsc`.                                              |
+| `bun run lint`         | Run ESLint.                                                         |
+| `bun run format:check` | Check formatting with Prettier (`format:fix` to rewrite).           |
+
+## API
+
+All endpoints are under `/api`. Request bodies are JSON (`content-type: application/json`).
+
+### Authentication
+
+Endpoints marked **auth** need an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. Use a seeded token or get one from `POST /api/auth/token`.
+
+- No or malformed header: `401` with `{"code":"unauthenticated","message":"missing bearer token"}`
+- Unknown or expired token: `401` with `Unauthorized`
+
+Authenticated requests only see resources in the caller's organization. Resources in other organizations return `404`.
+
+### Errors
+
+- A body that fails schema validation returns `422` with Elysia's validation error object (`type`, `on`, `property`, `message`, ...).
+- Most domain errors return `{"error": "<message>"}`. A few return plain text: `Project not found`, `Forbidden`, `invalid webhook secret`.
+- Unknown routes return `404` with `Not Found`.
+
+### Health
+
+#### `GET /api/health`
+
+Returns `200` with `{"status":"ok"}`.
+
+### Auth
+
+#### `POST /api/auth/token`
+
+Exchanges email and password for a new API token. Email matching is case-insensitive.
+
+```json
+{ "email": "ada@acme.test", "password": "password123" }
+```
+
+- `200`: `{"token": "...", "expiresAt": "<ISO timestamp>"}`. The token is valid for `TOKEN_TTL_HOURS`.
+- `401`: `{"error":"invalid email or password"}`
+
+#### `GET /api/me` (auth)
+
+Returns the current user:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "usr_ada",
+  "orgId": "org_acme",
+  "role": "admin",
+  "email": "ada@acme.test",
+  "name": "Ada Lovelace"
+}
+```
+
+### Projects
+
+#### `GET /api/projects` (auth)
+
+Lists the organization's projects sorted by name, with per-status task counts:
+
+```json
+{
+  "items": [
+    {
+      "id": "prj_web",
+      "name": "Website relaunch",
+      "description": "New marketing site",
+      "createdAt": "2026-11-15T20:46:01.235Z",
+      "taskCounts": { "todo": 1, "in_progress": 1, "done": 1 }
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+#### `POST /api/projects` (auth)
+
+| Field         | Type   | Required | Constraints      |
+| ------------- | ------ | -------- | ---------------- |
+| `name`        | string | yes      | 1 to 100 chars   |
+| `description` | string | no       | up to 2000 chars |
+
+Returns `201` with the project row (`id`, `orgId`, `name`, `description`, `createdAt`).
+
+#### `GET /api/projects/:id` (auth)
+
+Returns the project row, or `404` (`Project not found`).
+
+#### `GET /api/projects/:id/tasks` (auth)
+
+Returns `{"items": [Task, ...]}` for the project, oldest first. `404` if the project is not in the caller's organization.
+
+#### `POST /api/projects/:id/tasks` (auth)
+
+| Field         | Type    | Required | Constraints                                 |
+| ------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |
+| `title`       | string  | yes      | 1 to 200 chars                              |
+| `description` | string  | no       | up to 5000 chars                            |
+| `isUrgent`    | boolean | no       | defaults to `false`                         |
+| `assigneeId`  | string  | no       | must be a user in the caller's organization |
+| `dueDate`     | string  | no       | `YYYY-MM-DD`                                |
+
+New tasks start in `todo`. Returns `201` with the task.
+
+- `400`: `{"error":"assignee must be a member of your organization"}`
+- `404`: project not found
+
+If an assignee is set, they are sent an assignment email. Locally the mailer only logs a `mail.sent` line.
+
+### Tasks
+
+A task is returned in this shape:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "tsk_3",
+  "projectId": "prj_web",
+  "title": "Fix broken signup link",
+  "description": null,
+  "status": "todo",
+  "isUrgent": true,
+  "assigneeId": "usr_ada",
+  "dueDate": null,
+  "createdAt": "2026-10-01T09:03:00.000Z",
+  "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T09:03:00.000Z"
+}
+```
+
+`status` is one of `todo`, `in_progress` or `done`. `dueDate` is a `YYYY-MM-DD` string or `null`.
+
+#### `GET /api/tasks/:id` (auth)
+
+Returns the task, or `404` with `{"error":"task not found"}`.
+
+> **Known issue:** unlike the other endpoints, this one does not check the caller's organization. Any authenticated user can read any task by ID.
+
+#### `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` (auth)
+
+Partial update. All fields are optional:
+
+| Field         | Type                              | Notes                                                          |
+| ------------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `title`       | string                            | up to 200 chars. Trimmed and cannot be blank.                  |
+| `description` | string \| null                    | up to 5000 chars                                               |
+| `status`      | `todo` \| `in_progress` \| `done` | see the transition rules below                                 |
+| `isUrgent`    | boolean                           |                                                                |
+| `assigneeId`  | string \| null                    | must be a user in the caller's organization. `null` unassigns. |
+| `dueDate`     | string \| null                    | `YYYY-MM-DD`. `null` clears it.                                |
+
+Allowed status transitions:
+
+| From          | To                   |
+| ------------- | -------------------- |
+| `todo`        | `in_progress`        |
+| `in_progress` | `todo`, `done`       |
+| `done`        | `todo` (admins only) |
+
+Rules and errors:
+
+- `400`: blank title, or the assignee is not in the caller's organization.
+- `403`: a non-admin tries to reopen a `done` task.
+- `409`: the transition is not allowed, a task is marked `done` without an assignee (the assignee can be set in the same request), or a due date is set on a `done` task.
+- `404`: the task is not in the caller's organization.
+
+Returns `200` with the updated task. If nothing changes, the current task is returned and `updatedAt` stays the same. When the assignee changes to a user, that user is sent an assignment email.
+
+#### `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` (auth, admin only)
+
+- `204`: deleted
+- `403`: `Forbidden` (caller is not an admin)
+- `404`: `{"error":"task not found"}`
+
+### Webhooks
+
+#### `POST /api/webhooks/billing`
+
+Called by the billing provider. Requires the `x-webhook-secret` header to match `WEBHOOK_SECRET`. No bearer token is used.
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "evt_123",
+  "type": "payment.succeeded",
+  "data": { "orgId": "org_acme", "credits": 50 }
+}
+```
+
+- `data.credits` is an optional non-negative integer that defaults to `0`.
+- `payment.succeeded` adds `credits` to the organization's balance. Other event types are accepted and ignored.
+- `200`: `{"received":true}`
+- `401`: `invalid webhook secret`
+
+Example:
+
+```sh
+curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/webhooks/billing \
+  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
+  -H 'x-webhook-secret: change-me' \
+  -d '{"id":"evt_1","type":"payment.succeeded","data":{"orgId":"org_acme","credits":50}}'
+```
